{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>תּוֹרָה צִוָּה לָנוּ מֹשֶׁה</b> and so forth. There is a difficulty to note: since he himself is the one speaking, he should have said ״תּוֹרָה צִוִּיתִי לָכֶם״ and so forth. Perhaps it is because this verse follows from what precedes it, in this manner: the people of Israel will lift their voices from your words, all of them together as one voice: ״תּוֹרָה צִוָּה לָנוּ מֹשֶׁה״ and so forth — and these are likewise the words that all Israel together lift their voices in at the opening of the Torah." "<b>And His saying</b> ״תּוֹרָה צִוָּה לָנוּ״ and so forth — we accept it as a heritage of the congregation and so forth. And the meaning of ״צִוָּה לָנוּ״ may be interpreted as the might of kingship, as they said, of blessed memory: ״צַו״ means nothing other than kingship — for He enthroned it over us, so that a matter is established by its decree, and also the king whom they enthrone over themselves shall act by the authority of the Torah, and he shall write it and set it before him, as stated (Deuteronomy 17:18) ״וְכָתַב לוֹ״ and so forth. And this is the verse's statement (Proverbs 8:15) ״בִּי מְלָכִים יִמְלֹכוּ״. And above, at the verse ״אַף חֹבֵב״, we explained the verse in another manner, correctly."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:56.990602763Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}